          "id": "Nimpw",
          "name": "B",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-10-21 — Mirrored to code at 809ea789: Tu plan mirrored as built (D156) and its hub row moved after Apariencia, Resumen de Hoy switch, current-password field, API KEY label, Aperturas and last-sync lines on Estado, trace and log-module fixes, kit 1.3.0 TopBar search; drew Dos pasos activa, Verificando, Integraciones vacío, Registros filtrado and Mantenimiento activo; re-laid as bands Cuenta, Integraciones, Operación.\n2026-10-14 · kit 1.2.0 · Soft Candle wordmark in the TopBar at h-7; fg-subtle light #5E6E84; primary buttons on $primary-fg; BottomNav five equal slots\n2026-10-14 · En mantenimiento draws the shared wordmark at h-8 in place of the disc and typed name, as layouts/maintenance renders it\n2026-09-17 · D123: Alpha Vantage and FMP retired — their cards and manual-sync rows removed, source counts 10 → 8, the ProviderCard maintainer notice deleted; Estados draws sin cuota on ExchangeRate\n2026-09-16 · re-vendored to kit 1.0.0; BottomNav and SidebarNav masters had Ajustes lit, every screen now lights its own tab\n2026-09-16 · mirrored to the code (D78): hub sizes and copy, the phone switch, Integraciones rebuilt on a ProviderCard that carries state, quota bar, reason and the maintainer notice, Registros and Estado rebuilt, Errores rows and detail, En mantenimiento in its own chrome\n2026-09-16 · Integraciones · Administrar and Registros · Detalle drawn; the Hub, Integraciones and Estado desktops retired (D4) with the SidebarNav and TopBarDesktop they used\n2026-09-16 · code: the maintenance page lost its English navbar and footer; Estado stopped promising a banner and names each switch in its audit trail; the importer row describes Stockerly's own format; the empty Integraciones stopped sending an owner into the wizard; Registros keeps the task on its own line\n2026-09-16 · canvas on the grid; the brief rewritten into its fixed sections — its reasoning lives in D5, D16, D58, D78, D90, ADR-015, ADR-020 and git history\n2026-09-05 · En mantenimiento drawn — this flow owns the switch, and nothing drew what the switch causes\n2026-09-05 · that screen was the app's only English one, and the last to call its owner an administrator; fixed in code the same day\n2026-09-05 · A2 · Errores and Errores · Detalle drawn — the last undrawn surface in this flow\n2026-09-05 · D90 · Nombre y correo and Contraseña drawn — /profile retired, AJU-1 closed\n2026-09-05 · the desktop band reflowed: growing Hub · Desktop to 1235 had left it overlapping Integraciones · Desktop by 255px\n2026-09-05 · D78 · Tus datos draws the two real doors; the mailto and its 'pendiente' note are gone\n2026-09-05 · D78 · Zona horaria added to Apariencia y región; Errores row added to Tu instancia (ADR-020, conditional)\n2026-09-05 · D58 · the brief's open Guardar-vs-auto-save question closed — it shipped and the brief had not caught up\n2026-09-05 · Hub grows 1684 → 2140 to hold the two doors without clipping the BottomNav\n2026-08-29 · Tus datos gains an Importar movimientos NavRow — the section named how data leaves and never how it enters\n2026-08-29 · Yahoo's card on all three Integraciones artboards: it serves ticker search now, and its ceiling went 5 → 30 per minute · ADR-017 amendment\n2026-08-29 · this frame created; the brief still carries 7 dated lines from before it existed, not migrated yet\n2026-08-27 · kit 0.9.0 · HeaderBar promoted from four hand-built copies; BottomNav double active state fixed; Trabajos badge dropped; D52's Seguridad row added",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
